WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.212
SQL Server leans on certificates in three
places most retirement plans can't see.

2
00:00:05.212 --> 00:00:08.820
The TLS certificate every
Entra connection now requires,

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.750
since those connections
are always encrypted.

4
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.875
Certificates behind signed
code and endpoints.

5
00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:19.701
And certificate sign-in, the stopgap for
connections that can't reach Entra in time,

6
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:23.675
which quietly depends on the domain
controllers' own certificates.

7
00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:27.600
Cloud PKI can't help here;
it doesn't issue to servers.

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.571
The workbook's certificate plan settles
the issuer: a retained internal hierarchy,

9
00:00:32.571 --> 00:00:35.021
renewed through the lifecycle platform,

10
00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:39.200
with domain controller certificates
kept until the last one retires.

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.147
The decision for data leadership:
set no retirement date for the old

12
00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:47.375
certificate authority until every
SQL Server dependency has moved.

13
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:48.890
Then, what done means.
